ead1bf7f30bd4fd434889","position":"1785263342897340001-cb62ae76-ef8e-4c5a-be34-e5821f8d12c0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9b77fb2fa5ebf9f196554327a908af17426d35843e931916bac1bfac05d8ebc1","event_uuid":"24be9319-4a51-4e4a-bea9-6b4087deedfc","position":{"commit_sha":"3a9d81954534e9594c1ead1bf7f30bd4fd434889","position":"1785263343276506001-24be9319-4a51-4e4a-bea9-6b4087deedfc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Parent epic 1386 was remediated — read before implementing\n\nThe epic's AC1 was UNSATISFIABLE as written (it banned all SC vocabulary under `src/rebar/`\nwhile its own Scope deferred some) and has been amended. This does not change your scope, but\nit fixes what \"done\" means for the epic, and it names carve-outs you must NOT \"fix\":\n\n**Four permanent vocabulary carve-outs** — leave these exactly as they are:\n- `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T2.md` — \"a pilot with metrics, or stated success\n  criteria for a trial\". Generic English about an EXPERIMENT succeeding, not the ticket\n  heading. Story 2aa6's AC6 REQUIRES it to survive.\n- `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier.md`,\n  `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier_agentic.md`, and the `dod_uncertifiable` field\n  description in `src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify_models.py` — the\n  `dod_uncertifiable` / \"definition-of-done\" concept, which this epic explicitly defers.\n\n**Also amended:** epic AC5 now pins `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md` at EXACTLY ONE SC\nmatch (T2's echo) rather than zero — the guide is GENERATED from the criteria registry and\nembeds each criterion's prompt verbatim, so zero was impossible.\n\n**A gap was found and assigned to 5f4d, not to you:** `src/rebar/llm/completion.py:288`\n(\"its success criteria are met across children\") is genuine heading-sense vocabulary that no\nstory owned. It is now in 5f4d's scope. Don't pick it up here.\n\nPattern worth knowing before you write your own checks: four acceptance criteria in this epic\nso far (35bc AC1/AC3, 2aa6 AC1/AC3) were blanket string prohibitions that collided with their\nown deliberate exclusions, each needing a mid-implementation amendment and a re-review. If\nyour AC contains an absolute \"returns no matches\", check it against the exclusions first.","timestamp":1785018747323398001}],"created_at":1784944753898554001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6ad46a17-af03-420b-9106-94676e20a5a3","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"2aa6-726a-ea56-4d6c"},{"link_uuid":"b46c5a20-9997-4a03-9c07-1b5af6cbf5f8","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"35bc-aef6-efd5-4df5"}],"description":"## Why\n\nThe author-facing guides are the ONLY place the SC/AC split was ever described as a real\ndistinction — `rebar explain plan` currently tells container authors they need\n`## Success Criteria` on top of the universal `## Acceptance Criteria` floor. That prose is the\nsource of the divergence this epic removes; leaving it in place after the gates change would\ninstruct authors to write a heading nothing reads.\n\n## What\n\nRewrite the author guide and user docs for the collapsed vocabulary, including the leaf/container\nsection rule that motivated the split.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md:58,76` — the leaf-vs-container section rule\n  (\"Container ... needs `## Success Criteria`\" and \"Containers additionally: `## Success\n  Criteria` + the child decomposition\"). Both must be restated so containers are described by\n  what actually differs: they still need `## Acceptance Criteria`, plus a child decomposition\n  that COVERS it (G3), and they defer testing to children.\n- `docs/user-guide.md:219,230`\n- `docs/llm-framework.md:407`\n\n## Approach\n\nRewrite rather than substitute. A literal rename of line 58 would read \"Container needs\n`## Acceptance Criteria`\", which is true of every ticket and so says nothing — the container\nguidance has to be re-expressed as the decomposition/coverage requirement. This is the one place\nin the epic where the edit is editorial rather than mechanical.\n\nNote the guide is packaged and surfaced by `rebar explain plan`, so it is a shipped artifact,\nnot just documentation.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `rebar explain plan` renders the updated guide with no SC vocabulary.\n- `pytest tests -k \"guide or explain\"` green.\n- Manual read-through that the container guidance still tells an author what containers need\n  DIFFERENTLY from leaves (coverage + decomposition), i.e. the section did not become vacuous.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `grep -rniE \"success[ _-]criteri(a|on)\" src/rebar/_guides/ docs/user-guide.md docs/llm-framework.md` returns no matches.\n- [ ] `rebar explain plan` exits 0 and its output contains no SC vocabulary.\n- [ ] The guide's leaf-vs-container section still states a container-specific requirement\n      (child decomposition covering the parent's acceptance criteria, testing deferred to\n      children) rather than collapsing to \"containers need Acceptance Criteria\".\n- [ ] `make lint` and the full pytest suite pass.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md","reason":"Rewrite the leaf-vs-container section rule"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"Clarity and verify-completion prose"},{"path":"docs/llm-framework.md","reason":"Parent-criteria prose"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","2aa6-726a-ea56-4d6c"],["depends_on","35bc-aef6-efd5-4df5"],["parent","1386-5e7c-391d-4a74"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"1386-5e7c-391d-4a74","parent_status_uuid":"cb62ae76-ef8e-4c5a-be34-e5821f8d12c0","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["vocabulary","plan-review"],"ticket_id":"44c7-0cbd-4d47-4f5f","ticket_type":"story","title":"Rewrite author guide and user docs for the collapsed criteria vocabulary","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["73012b3a-6627-4761-a721-d1e82455028e","6ad46a17-af03-420b-9106-94676e20a5a3","b46c5a20-9997-4a03-9c07-1b5af6cbf5f8","462b5ae1-1e2e-4b88-be6d-f3e3bf382cde","3cab5e0a-5544-4fef-9539-50d003a0dcc4","b9f96cf3-d58a-4695-9a8f-26d0c9ed576b","7f7036f4-b304-4940-b24b-e96661c0ccd4","cb62ae76-ef8e-4c5a-be34-e5821f8d12c0","24be9319-4a51-4e4a-bea9-6b4087deedfc"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785263343276506002,"uuid":"9874e5a0-4d0a-4ece-926b-ba7b149224c5"}